  "description": "Radio-frequency front-end design: cryogenic low-noise amplifiers with 20-50 K noise temperature (closed-cycle helium or Stirling cooled for DSN-grade apertures), downconverters that mix the RF to intermediate frequency, and the IF distribution that carries signals to a signal processing centre over fibre or coax. The subsystem that sets the system noise temperature and therefore the link budget.",
